  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">World Bank Umbrella Facility for Trade</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Australia&apos;s contribution to the World Bank Umbrella Facility for Trade supports economic recovery from Covid-19 through trade. It supports developing countries in the Indo-Pacific to align their trade practices with the WTO Trade Facilitation Agreement, helping identify constraints to cross-border trade, supporting reforms, and helping increase the predictability, transparency, and harmonisation of customs procedures and transit standards. The investment also supports developing countries to participate in digital trade by assisting them to develop policy and regulatory frameworks conducive to digital trade and supports participation in the WTO Joint Statement Initiative on E-commerce.</narrative>
  </description>
